{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791294180,"nonce":"TMUOKlmR/x/UJidYreMrp6TyFjw=","title":"HIR inliner treats scalar floor as a runtime call","message":"Intrinsic::Floor is in the runtime-trampoline category even though it reads one numeric operand and has no runtime memory effects. Sin, Cos, Sqrt and other scalar math intrinsics are already classified as leaf work. Floor makes Lua exact integer/float comparison helpers count as call-bearing, so the caller budget rejects zl_lt_fi in Mandelbrot after constructors have inlined. Classify Floor consistently with the other scalar math intrinsics; keep real runtime calls under their existing budgets.\n\nThe shared HIR then inlines and folds the comparison against a constant integer bound to a direct float comparison. Eighteen inliner unit tests pass, including an inlined negative floor execution through the interpreter. LLVM-feature Lua/Python conformance passes (43 Lua tests excluding official suites; 50 Python tests). Five alternating NUC processes across all 17 Lua kernels produced correct checksums. Mandelbrot kernel 47.977 to 46.838 ms, wall 95.312 to 92.413 ms, only a small gain; no broad speed claim. Tokenize 175.488 to 170.560 ms, while any_field kernel 0.968 to 2.049 ms (wall 26.566 to 27.642 ms). Full measurements: /tmp/zyntax-nuc-floor-lua-ab.json on the NUC.","files":null}]}